---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Lubie"
  category="Project | Intelligent Lubrication System"
  year="2026"
  description="Adaptive machining lubrication system managing tool length, lubrication mode, tool orientation and cutting engagement."
>

  <p slot="intro">
    An adaptive lubrication concept designed to automatically position and control
    coolant delivery according to tool geometry, machining conditions and cutting engagement.
  </p>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      01
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Objective
      </h2>

      <p>
        Lubie is an automated machining lubrication system designed to continuously
        adapt coolant delivery to the actual cutting situation.
      </p>

      <p>
        Instead of relying on a fixed nozzle position, the system aims to manage
        tool length, lubrication mode, nozzle orientation and tool penetration
        into the material.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      02
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Adaptive positioning
      </h2>

      <p>
        The lubrication head is intended to automatically reposition itself
        according to the active tool geometry.
      </p>

      <p>
        Tool length is taken into account so that the lubrication point remains
        correctly positioned after tool changes without requiring manual adjustment.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Automatic adaptation to tool length
        </li>

        <li>
          Controlled nozzle orientation
        </li>

        <li>
          Position adjustment according to the machining zone
        </li>

        <li>
          Continuous targeting of the cutting interface
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      03
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Lubrication modes
      </h2>

      <p>
        The concept is designed to support several lubrication strategies depending
        on machining requirements.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          MQL | Minimum Quantity Lubrication
        </li>

        <li>
          Conventional coolant delivery
        </li>

        <li>
          High-flow lubrication
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The objective is to allow the machine to select or switch between lubrication
        modes according to the operation, material and thermal requirements.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      04
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Tool orientation
      </h2>

      <p>
        On multi-axis machines, the relative orientation between the tool,
        workpiece and lubrication nozzle changes continuously.
      </p>

      <p>
        Lubie therefore integrates controlled orientation around the tool in order
        to maintain an effective lubrication direction during complex machining paths.
      </p>

      <p>
        The system is intended to follow changes in tool orientation rather than
        remaining fixed relative to the machine structure.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      05
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Cutting engagement
      </h2>

      <p>
        The lubrication strategy is also intended to account for tool penetration
        into the material.
      </p>

      <p>
        As cutting engagement changes, the optimal direction, distance and flow
        requirement of the lubrication system may also change.
      </p>

      <p>
        The objective is therefore to adapt coolant delivery dynamically according
        to the actual cutting condition instead of using a constant setting.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      06
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Mechanical architecture
      </h2>

      <p>
        The concept requires a compact orientation mechanism capable of moving
        around the spindle while maintaining fluid supply.
      </p>

      <p>
        A rotary fluid connection can be used to allow continuous or extended
        angular motion without twisting the lubrication hoses.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Rotational axis around the spindle
        </li>

        <li>
          Secondary orientable nozzle axis
        </li>

        <li>
          Rotary fluid union
        </li>

        <li>
          Variable nozzle position
        </li>

        <li>
          Adjustable flow and jet length
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      07
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Control strategy
      </h2>

      <p>
        The lubrication system can be linked to machining information already
        available in the CNC environment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Tool identification, tool length, spindle orientation, machine axes and
        machining parameters can provide the information required to determine
        the lubrication configuration.
      </p>

      <p>
        The long-term objective is to make lubrication an adaptive machine function
        rather than a manually adjusted peripheral system.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      08
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Design goals
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Improve lubrication precision
        </li>

        <li>
          Reduce manual nozzle adjustment
        </li>

        <li>
          Adapt automatically after tool changes
        </li>

        <li>
          Support multiple lubrication technologies
        </li>

        <li>
          Follow multi-axis tool orientation
        </li>

        <li>
          Adapt flow to cutting engagement
        </li>

        <li>
          Improve machining repeatability
        </li>

        <li>
          Reduce unnecessary coolant consumption
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      09
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Vision
      </h2>

      <p>
        Lubie explores the idea of treating lubrication as an actively controlled
        machining parameter rather than a fixed auxiliary function.
      </p>

      <p>
        By combining tool data, machine kinematics and adaptive fluid delivery,
        the system could provide more consistent lubrication across increasingly
        complex machining operations.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>

</ProjectLayout>